Data terms for SynthGuard

1. Source images and labels
   a) Main dataset: "construction safety" from the Roboflow 100 benchmark
      (Roboflow Universe, exported 2023-01-27, "v1 release-640"), mirrored on the
      Hugging Face Hub as Francesco/construction-safety-gsnvb
      (revision cd92c83884cc7c0ba1a3fda584784f550321e16f).
      License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Attribution: Roboflow 100 /
      Roboflow Universe contributors. Changes made by SynthGuard: labels remapped
      (no-helmet -> head; vest classes dropped), derived images produced as below.
   b) Archived dataset (v0.1 runs): Voxel51/hard-hat-detection
      (revision d11e7d6b69ba1a22422db3230c0415d39a699d7c), declared CC0-1.0.
   SynthGuard does not redistribute either dataset; `synthguard download` fetches them.

2. Derived images (classic augmentation, copy-paste)
   Inherit the terms of their source images: CC BY 4.0 with attribution for the main
   dataset, CC0-1.0 for the archived one.

3. Diffusion images (optional)
   Contain synthetic persons; no real identity is intentionally depicted.
   When generated with FLUX.1-dev or its control LoRAs, they are subject to the
   FLUX.1 [dev] Non-Commercial License: do not sell or package them as a commercial
   dataset. The SDXL dev proxy (SDXL base 1.0, CreativeML Open RAIL++-M) is used only
   to test the pipeline on the development machine.
   When generated with Krea 2 Turbo (the img2img stand-in for E1 and the text-to-image
   scene batches), they are subject to that model's own license, which this project
   has not reviewed. Check it before using such images beyond evaluation.
   None of these weights or generated images are distributed with SynthGuard.

4. assets/examples/
   At most 20 triptychs built from main-dataset images (CC BY 4.0, attribution
   above) and SynthGuard outputs.

The code license (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE) does not change any of the above.
